## 7. Phase B — Verify Live U02 OPC Data

Confirm that MFCS_OPCUA is connected and U02 returns valid live values.

The previously verified addressing convention is:

`nsu=http://www.sartorius.com/BioPAT_MFCS_OPC_Server/Units;s=U02.TEMP.Value`

Verify each actual NodeId against the existing discovery evidence and current OPC server.

The proposed live mapping is:

| Existing UDT Member | MFCS OPC Identifier |
|---|---|
| TEMP | U02.TEMP.Value |
| pH | U02.pH.Value |
| pO2 | U02.pO2.Value |
| AFOAMT | U02.AFOAMT.Value |
| BASET | U02.BASET.Value |
| SUBS_A | U02.SUBS_A.Value |
| SUBS_B | U02.SUBS_B.Value |
| SUBS_C | U02.SUBS_C.Value |
| VWEIGHT | U02.VWEIGHT.Value |
| JTEMP | U02.JTEMP.Value |
| AIROV | U02.AIROV.Value |
| STIRR | U02.STIRR.Value |

Use the complete verified namespace URI-based NodeIds when configuring Ignition.

For every parameter:

- Confirm the OPC NodeId.
- Confirm current value.
- Confirm valid data quality.
- Confirm engineering units.
- Confirm data type compatibility.
- Confirm parameter semantics.
- Confirm that the address references U02 rather than U01.

Do not treat Good_NoData or other unavailable data statuses as valid live measurements.

Do not reject an otherwise valid static measurement solely because it does not change during the observation period.

### Parameters excluded from this commission

Leave the following parameters unchanged pending engineering reconciliation:

- CO2SP
- AIRSP
- N2SP
- O2SP

Do not implement undocumented engineering unit conversions or substitute controller process values for setpoints.

## 8. Phase C — Implement Minimum Instance-Level Changes

Apply the same successful source integration approach used in Commission 06A.

Modify only the required properties of existing BRX5-02-02 members:

| Property | Authorized change |
|---|---|
| opcServer | Set to MFCS_OPCUA |
| opcItemPath | Set to verified U02 NodeId |
| valueSource | Change to OPC only where required |
| enabled | Enable verified live process members |

For STIRR, verify whether the existing source is a memory tag before converting it to OPC.

Preserve all other effective member properties.

Use supported Ignition configuration merge operations. Do not replace the entire equipment instance.

Ensure simulation scripts or writers cannot overwrite transitioned live measurements.

Do not modify shared simulation logic or disable simulation for unrelated equipment.

Apply a small initial subset of verified parameters if needed to establish the correct configuration mechanism, then expand to all 12 eligible parameters on the same equipment instance.

After applying the changes, re-export the equipment instance and verify the actual property-level differences.

