## 14. Operating Restrictions

The following activities are prohibited:

- Equipment control commands.
- OPC process writes.
- Starting or stopping equipment operation.
- Modifying process setpoints.
- Changing parent UDT definitions.
- Modifying equipment hierarchy.
- Modifying SCADA graphics or bindings.
- Modifying alarm definitions or thresholds.
- Enabling unauthorized alarm notifications.
- Modifying historical collection configuration.
- Changing equipment images or colors.
- Modifying unrelated equipment instances.
- Changing certificates or authentication settings.
- Restarting the Ignition Gateway.
- Deploying new equipment UDTs.
- Deploying additional Ignition projects.
- Deploying automatic rollback guards.
- Automatically substituting simulated values during communication failures.

Verify that the monitoring integration cannot inadvertently execute equipment commands or write process values back to MFCS.

If an unauthorized downstream effect is identified, stop the affected operation and document the required mitigation.

## 15. Mandatory Final Equipment Enablement and Disposition

**This section is mandatory and takes precedence over any earlier commissioning instruction to disable or restore simulation at completion.**

The objective is to leave both BIOSTAT Twin vessels enabled and available for Acropolis visual verification.

Before completing the commission, verify the following final state:

| Configuration | BRX5-02-01 | BRX5-02-02 |
|---|---|---|
| MFCS source | U01 — Left Twin | U02 — Right Twin |
| OPC connection | MFCS_OPCUA | MFCS_OPCUA |
| EquipIsEnabled | 1 | 1 |
| Live process members | 12 | 12 |
| Enabled KeyCPP references | 3 | 3 |
| Simulation on transitioned tags | Off | Off |
| Source quality | Good when source available | Good when source available |
| Automatic rollback guard | Not active | Not active |
| Final disposition | Leave enabled | Leave enabled |

Do not revert either equipment instance to simulation or a disabled state upon commission completion.

Verify that the temporary Commission 06A rollback guard, TBMC_COM06A_PilotGuard_0224, remains retired and cannot undo the successful live integrations.

Do not deploy another automatic rollback guard.

Ignition or Kymera trial expiration must not cause the live OPC configuration to be removed.

Retain the configured addresses and administrative equipment enablement through temporary communications interruptions.

If OPC communication is interrupted:

- Retain the live OPC configuration.
- Allow existing quality and availability logic to reflect the interruption.
- Do not substitute simulated process measurements.
- Do not artificially force a Good source quality indication.
- Allow normal OPC reconnection and data recovery.

Leave both vessels enabled and configured for live SCADA monitoring, subject to the authorized commissioning conditions.

Maintain a targeted manual rollback package, but do not execute rollback solely because the commission has completed.

Execute rollback only if an unauthorized configuration change, equipment control risk or other unacceptable operational effect occurs.

**Capture a final screenshot showing both bioreactors displaying live measurements simultaneously on the existing Plasmid-814 overview.**

The commission shall not be reported as fully passed unless this final visual state has been demonstrated.

